          <p style="font-weight: var(--font-weight-semibold); font-size: var(--text-regular); margin: 0 0 var(--space-4);">Our Approach</p>
          <h2 style="font-size: var(--text-h2); line-height: var(--text-h2-line-height); letter-spacing: var(--heading-letter-spacing); font-weight: var(--font-weight-bold); margin: 0 0 var(--space-6); text-wrap: pretty;">We treat AI in education as a science, not a gold rush.</h2>
          <p style="font-size: var(--text-medium); line-height: var(--text-body-line-height); margin: 0px; text-wrap: pretty;">We run an iterative research and development cycle, with educators, researchers, and engineers as equal partners at every step. We start by asking what teachers and students need. Each cycle focuses on one role AI could play in meeting some of those needs. Together, we identify what the role requires but doesn't yet exist, build it, and test it in real classrooms. What we learn informs the next turn of the cycle.</p>
